{
    "pageid": 2741,
    "title": "Merging guide",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "This guide describes the steps to retrofit the changes from a vanilla patch , for a mod that modifies some vanilla files."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "It is best to avoid copying and modifying vanilla files inside a mod (by loading from folders ), but sometimes this is unavoidable."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "If you do, there is some extra work needed for every vanilla patch, to merge changes with your own, and make the mod compatible with the new patch:"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Merge tool",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Ideally you should use a 3-way merge tool, with 3-way folder merging capability:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "3-way text merging will resolve most conflicts automatically, allowing to complete much faster and with less risks of mistakes.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "3-way folder merging allows to trigger the 3-way text merge of files that need merging more conveniently.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Some 3-way merge tools:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "KDiff3",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Beyond Compare 4 Pro (30 days free trial)",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Note that WinMerge doesn't support 3-way merge, only 2-way diff."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Launching the merge",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "3-way merge is composed of 4 windows:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Source : The mod",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Base : The last vanilla version for which the mod was updated for",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Destination : The vanilla version to updated to",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Result : The mod",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "For simplicity, it's common to have source and result work on same files, but make sure the old version of the mod is backed-up in case you need to re-start the merge for any reason."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": ""
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "",
                            "This article is a Stub ,  which means that it does not sufficiently cover its subject matter. Please help expand this article if you can."
                        ]
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": ""
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Tips",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Tell the mergetool about CK2 syntax, for an even more efficient merge and some syntax coloration:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Comment = Text from # to end of line",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Identifier = Text matching [_a-z]\\w*",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "String = Text from \" to \"",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "...",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "If possible, add new mod entities in separate files, as things added at the end of a vanilla files will always conflict when new elements are added to vanilla.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "If removing elements from a large vanilla file, leave breadcrumbs to help the merge tool. This will prevent the tool from attempting to merge with the next element in the file.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "For instance if removing religious CB in 00_cb_types, keeping the following in the mod will help future merges:"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
